      "message": "//It is only passed through, so there is no need to know the specific structure type.\n\nstruct loop_device; \nstruct loop_worker;\n\nstruct oplus_loop_ext {\n        struct work_struct      work;\n        struct list_head        cmd_list;\n        struct loop_device *lo;\n};\n\nin vendor hook,  we  use like:\n     disk \u003d rq-\u003eq-\u003edisk;\n     ext \u003d (struct oplus_loop_ext *)disk-\u003eandroid_oem_data1; //The ext and its\u0027 work is allocated/init at other locations\n     cmd \u003d blk_mq_rq_to_pdu(rq);\n                ext-\u003elo \u003d lo;\n    list_add_tail((struct list_head *)cmd, \u0026ext-\u003ecmd_list);\n  queue_work(oplus_kverityd_wq, \u0026ext-\u003ework); //oplus_kverityd_wq have high prio kthreads. \n\nwork is like this:\nstatic void oplus_loop_workfn(struct work_struct *work)\n{\n        struct oplus_loop_ext *ext \u003d (struct oplus_loop_ext *)work;\n        loop_process_cmd_list(NULL, \u0026ext-\u003ecmd_list, ext-\u003elo);\n}",
